{%- comment -%}
  Cart overlap guard — store-wide.

  WHY THIS IS NOT PART OF THE BUNDLE LADDER. The ladder can only police the adds it
  handles itself. A shopper who takes the Complete Library from its own page and then
  walks to the Intrusive Thoughts Bundle and uses the main Add to cart never touches the
  ladder, and ends up holding both — which is the same broken promise the ladder was
  fixed to stop making, arrived at from the other direction. Upsell apps, quick-add,
  product cards and a cart restored from a previous session are all the same hole.

  So the rule lives with the cart instead of with any one button. It is rendered from
  layout/theme.liquid on every template, it re-checks after every cart change from any
  source, and it also checks on page load, which is what catches a cart that became
  redundant in another tab or on a previous visit.

  WHERE THE TRUTH LIVES. On the product, not in this file and not in a template: the
  `custom.bundle_includes` metafield on a bundle lists the products that bundle contains.
  One place to edit, and every surface — this guard, the ladder, anything added later —
  reads the same answer. A bundle with an empty metafield is inert: nothing about the
  cart changes until a merchant states what a bundle actually contains.

  THIS FILE NAMES BOTH SIDES, IT DOES NOT PICK ONE. Every overlap is emitted as a pair:
  the `contained` line and the `container` line that swallows it. Which one leaves is a
  question about what the shopper just did, and Liquid cannot see that — the cart looks
  identical whichever way round it was built. bundle-overlap.js diffs the cart to work
  out which side is the new arrival and drops the other. Deciding here would have baked
  in "the big one always wins", which is exactly the bug this replaced: a shopper who
  already had the Library and deliberately chose the smaller bundle watched their click
  do nothing at all.

  MUTUAL CONTAINMENT IS REFUSED. If two products each claim to include the other, that is
  a data-entry mistake, and honouring it would remove both and hand the shopper an empty
  cart. Neither is touched, so the mistake shows up as "nothing happened" rather than as
  a vanished order.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pairs = ''
  assign products = ''

  for item in cart.items
    if products != blank
      assign products = products | append: ','
    endif
    assign products = products | append: item.product.id

    assign container_found = false
    assign container_key = ''
    assign container_variant = 0
    assign container_quantity = 0
    assign container_product = 0
    assign container_title = ''

    for other in cart.items
      unless other.key == item.key
        assign other_includes_item = false
        for included in other.product.metafields.custom.bundle_includes.value
          if included.id == item.product.id
            assign other_includes_item = true
            break
          endif
        endfor

        assign item_includes_other = false
        for included in item.product.metafields.custom.bundle_includes.value
          if included.id == other.product.id
            assign item_includes_other = true
            break
          endif
        endfor

        if other_includes_item
          unless item_includes_other
            comment
              Captured field by field: `other` is the loop variable, and reading it after
              the break is not something to rely on.
            endcomment
            assign container_found = true
            assign container_key = other.key
            assign container_variant = other.variant_id
            assign container_quantity = other.quantity
            assign container_product = other.product.id
            assign container_title = other.product.title
            break
          endunless
        endif
      endunless
    endfor

    if container_found
      capture pair
        echo '{"contained":{"key":'
        echo item.key | json
        echo ',"variant_id":'
        echo item.variant_id
        echo ',"quantity":'
        echo item.quantity
        echo ',"product_id":'
        echo item.product.id
        echo ',"title":'
        echo item.product.title | json
        echo '},"container":{"key":'
        echo container_key | json
        echo ',"variant_id":'
        echo container_variant
        echo ',"quantity":'
        echo container_quantity
        echo ',"product_id":'
        echo container_product
        echo ',"title":'
        echo container_title | json
        echo '}}'
      endcapture

      if pairs != blank
        assign pairs = pairs | append: ','
      endif
      assign pairs = pairs | append: pair
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  `lines` lets the script refuse a verdict that would empty the cart outright, and
  `products` is what it diffs against the previous check to spot the new arrival.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/json" data-blo-verdict>{"lines":{{ cart.items.size }},"products":[{{ products }}],"pairs":[{{ pairs }}]}</script>

{%- if section.settings.enabled -%}
  <script
    type="module"
    src="{{ 'bundle-overlap.js' | asset_url }}"
    fetchpriority="low"
  ></script>

  <bundle-overlap
    data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
    data-cart-url="{{ routes.cart_url }}"
    data-add-url="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
    data-update-url="{{ routes.cart_update_url }}"
    data-mode="{{ section.settings.mode }}"
    data-removed-message="{{ section.settings.removed_message | escape }}"
    data-swapped-message="{{ section.settings.swapped_message | escape }}"
    data-ask-message="{{ section.settings.ask_message | escape }}"
    data-undo-label="{{ section.settings.undo_label | escape }}"
    data-remove-label="{{ section.settings.remove_label | escape }}"
    {% if request.design_mode %}data-design-mode{% endif %}
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      `popover` puts the notice in the browser's top layer. Without it the message loses
      a race it cannot win: adding from the main buy button opens the cart drawer, which
      is a modal <dialog>, and a modal dialog paints above every z-index on the page. The
      notice was rendering correctly and sitting behind the drawer, which is why removals
      made from the buy button looked silent. `manual` keeps light-dismiss off so a stray
      tap cannot take the Undo away with it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="blo" role="status" aria-live="polite" popover="manual" hidden data-blo-toast>
      <p class="blo__text" data-blo-text></p>
      <div class="blo__actions">
        <button type="button" class="blo__action" data-blo-action hidden></button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="blo__dismiss"
          data-blo-dismiss
          aria-label="{{ 'actions.close' | t | default: 'Close' }}"
        >
          &times;
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </bundle-overlap>

  {%- style -%}
    bundle-overlap { display: contents; }

    /*
      Pinned to the top, under the header. A cart notice belongs where the cart is: the
      bottom of the screen is where a shopper on a phone has their thumb, the sticky
      add-to-cart bar, and the browser chrome — three things competing with a message
      they get one chance to read.

      Every UA popover default is restated: `inset`, `margin`, `border`, `padding` and
      `background` all come pre-set on [popover] and would otherwise fight these.
    */
    .blo {
      position: fixed;
      inset: auto;
      top: calc(var(--header-height, 60px) + 12px);
      left: 12px;
      right: 12px;
      width: auto;
      max-width: 30rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
      z-index: 2147483000;
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 12px;
      padding: 12px 12px 12px 14px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--color-background, #0B0F0D);
      color: var(--color-foreground, #fff);
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgb(0 0 0 / 34%);
      font-size: .82rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
      overflow: visible;
    }
    .blo[hidden] { display: none; }
    .blo:not(:popover-open) { display: none; }

    .blo__text { margin: 0; flex: 1 1 auto; }
    .blo__actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; flex: 0 0 auto; }

    .blo__action {
      background: none; border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 4px 2px;
      font: inherit; font-weight: 700;
      color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
      cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .blo__action[hidden] { display: none; }

    .blo__dismiss {
      background: none; border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0;
      width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 999px;
      font: inherit; font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1;
      color: inherit; opacity: .6; cursor: pointer;
    }
    .blo__dismiss:hover { opacity: 1; }

    .blo__action:focus-visible,
    .blo__dismiss:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 2px; }

    @media (min-width: 750px) {
      .blo { left: auto; right: 20px; margin-inline: 0; }
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart overlap guard",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Keeps the cart from holding a bundle and something that bundle already contains. List a bundle's contents in its \"Bundle includes\" metafield — with no metafield set, this does nothing. Whichever product the shopper added last is the one that stays."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enabled", "label": "Enabled", "default": true },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "mode",
      "label": "When the cart holds an overlap",
      "options": [
        { "value": "remove", "label": "Remove it, with an Undo" },
        { "value": "ask", "label": "Ask before removing" }
      ],
      "default": "remove",
      "info": "Choose \"Ask\" where a bundle only partly covers the other product, so the shopper decides whether to give it up."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "removed_message",
      "label": "Message when the smaller item is removed",
      "default": "[items] came out of your cart — [bundle] already includes it.",
      "info": "Shown when the shopper adds the bigger bundle. [items] is what was removed, [bundle] is what stayed."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "swapped_message",
      "label": "Message when the bundle is removed",
      "default": "[items] came out of your cart — it already includes [kept], which you just added.",
      "info": "Shown when the shopper deliberately adds the smaller product instead. [items] is what was removed, [kept] is what they just added."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "ask_message",
      "label": "Message when asking",
      "default": "[bundle] already includes [items]. Take it out of your cart?"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "undo_label", "label": "Undo button label", "default": "Undo" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "remove_label", "label": "Remove button label", "default": "Remove it" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Cart overlap guard" }]
}
{% endschema %}
